        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-04T17:31:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question. Based on my interpretation of the specification [0], \"aud\" is the intended audience of the token. In the case of OpenStack, would that be the user or service users?\n\nI\u0027m not sure what we would put here since multiple actors can validate a token (e.g., administrators, services users, users themselves).\n\nOpenStack audit IDs are a bit different and specific to OpenStack in my opinion. I\u0027m not sure they exactly match up with any of the claims described in the specification, but I\u0027m curious if you have a different view point.\n\n[0] https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7519#section-4.1.3",
      "parentUuid": "9fdfeff1_aea049f5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 122,
        "endChar": 32
      },
